raw industrial power.\n\n**Frames 267–271:** At 267 seconds, the scene cuts abruptly to a pristine indoor exhibition hall displaying a massive turbofan jet engine. The engine—featuring a distinctive green fan section with visible blades, silver metallic casing, and complex internal piping—rests on white conical supports. Behind it, a curved blue wall displays a large white stylized logo (resembling the Rostec or United Engine Corporation emblem). The setting is clean, brightly lit, and controlled, with no visible human activity. This static display showcases precision engineering and technological sophistication, creating a mood of technical advancement and manufacturing excellence in stark contrast to the fiery chaos of the preceding frames.', 'similarity score': 0.43726301193237305}, {'clip_334_343': 'clip_334_343', 'text': '**334s:** The sequence opens with a scenic view of **Mt. Hoverla (2,061 m)**—a prominent, grass-covered mountain peak under a bright blue sky with scattered white clouds. Rocky terrain is visible in the foreground, and yellow text at the bottom identifies the location and elevation.\n\n**335s–343s:** The scene transitions to a static, picturesque view of a **mountain village** nestled in rolling green hills. The composition features:\n- **Buildings:** Several rustic houses with dark roofs scattered across the slopes, plus a distinctive **yellow church with multiple onion domes** (suggesting Eastern Orthodox architecture) perched on a higher hill in the background.\n- **Rural elements:** Traditional haystacks dot the grassy fields, and a white vehicle is visible near the church.\n- **Landscape:** Lush green pastures, scattered evergreen trees, and power lines running across the upper hillside under a clear, sunny sky.\n\n**Mood:** The sequence conveys **tranquility and pastoral beauty**, contrasting the grandeur of the highest peak with the peaceful, timeless quality of rural mountain life. No significant motion occurs in the village frames, su